    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Franklin Carlock founded the village on January 5, 1888, after laying out a new town a mile and a half from his original site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlock%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Carlock boasted twenty dwellings, a town hall, two general stores, a blacksmith, a steam mill, a harness shop, and a brass band.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlock%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Residents once argued that the town’s only need was a railroad, a sentiment echoed by a reporter at the time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlock%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village’s guiding principles emphasize small‑town values, guided growth, and preservation of its historical, cultural, and natural heritage.",
